<title>FRANCE: Sommer Allibert sells bathrooms unit.</title>
<headline>Sommer Allibert sells bathrooms unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial supplier Sommer Allibert said on Thursday that it would sell its bathrooms business to private U.S. investment fund Andlinger for 260 million francs.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it decided to sell the business as part of its strategy to focus on its core activities and that it would apply the proceeds to reducing its debt.</p>
<p>The bathrooms business generated sales of 660 million francs last year, Sommer Allibert said. It said a preliminary agreement had been signed and the deal was expected to close before the end of February.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
